    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\alpha=1,\\ \\beta=2,\\ \\gamma=3$.\n\nUse the power sums to form $x^3-6x^2+11x-6=0$ and factorise.",
      "worked": "Let $u=\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma$ and $v=\\alpha\\beta\\gamma$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u&=\\frac{(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)^2-(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2)}{2}\\\\u&=\\frac{6^2-14}{2}\\\\u&=11.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe roots satisfy $x^3-6x^2+11x-v=0$. Substitute each root and add the three equations:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha^3+\\beta^3+\\gamma^3-6(\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2)+11(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)-3v&=0\\\\36-6(14)+11(6)-3v&=0\\\\18-3v&=0\\\\v&=6.\\end{align*}$$\n\nHence the cubic is\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x^3-6x^2+11x-6&=0\\\\(x-1)(x^2-5x+6)&=0\\\\(x-1)(x-2)(x-3)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\n\nIts roots are $1,2,3$. Since $\\alpha<\\beta<\\gamma$, $\\alpha=1$, $\\beta=2$ and $\\gamma=3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
